    "text": "To determine how many liters of oil the store owner had, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total volume of oil in milliliters.\n2. Convert the total volume from milliliters to liters.\n\nFirst, we know that the store owner repacked his oils into 200 mL bottles and was able to make 20 bottles. Therefore, the total volume of oil is:\n\\[ 200 \\text{ mL/bottle} \\times 20 \\text{ bottles} = 4000 \\text{ mL} \\]\n\nNext, we need to convert the total volume from milliliters to liters. Since there are 1000 milliliters in a liter, we divide the total volume in milliliters by 1000:\n\\[ 4000 \\text{ mL} \\div 1000 = 4 \\text{ L} \\]\n\nThus, the store owner had \\(\\boxed{4}\\) liters of oil.",
